e=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Rice vinegar</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">3</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cloves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Garlic, minced</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Fresh ginger, grated</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Chili flakes</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Black pepper</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Green onions, sliced</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For garnish</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-3370-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3370\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing the marinade</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Resealable bag or bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For marinating the chicken</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Grill or Oven&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For cooking the chicken</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-3370-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-3370-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3370\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation Steps</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3370-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">In a bowl, whisk together soy sauce, sesame oil, honey, and rice vinegar until well combined.</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3370-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Add minced garlic, grated ginger, chili flakes, and black pepper to the bowl. Stir to combine all those wonderful flavors.</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3370-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Place your chicken in a resealable bag or bowl. Pour the marinade over the chicken, ensuring it’s well coated.</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3370-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Seal the bag or cover the bowl. Refrigerate for at least 1 hour, or overnight for maximum flavor.</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3370-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Preheat your grill or oven to medium-high heat. Get ready for some sizzling action!</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3370-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Take the chicken out of the marinade and shake off any excess. We want it flavorful, not swimming!</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3370-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Grill or bake the chicken until it’s cooked through and the internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C). You’ve got this!</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3370-step-0-7\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Garnish with sliced green onions and serve hot. Enjoy your delicious creation!</div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-3370-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>200</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>8g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>20g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>10g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Check out these simple ingredients for a delicious Asian marinade for <a href=\"https://www.fsis.usda.gov/sites/default/files/media_file/2020-10/Chicken_Turkey_Nutrition_Facts.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">chicken</a>!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Asian-Marinade-for-Chicken.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for an asian marinade for chicken displayed on a wooden kitchen table, including soy sauce, sesame oil, honey, rice vinegar, garlic, ginger, chili flakes, black pepper, and green onions.\" class=\"wp-image-3368\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Asian-Marinade-for-Chicken.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Asian-Marinade-for-Chicken-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Soy sauce</strong> – 1/2 cup</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Sesame oil</strong> – 2 tablespoons</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Honey</strong> – 2 tablespoons</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Rice vinegar</strong> – 2 tablespoons</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Garlic, minced</strong> – 3 cloves</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Fresh ginger, grated</strong> – 1 tablespoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Chili flakes</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Black pepper</strong> – 1/2 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Green onions, sliced</strong> – 2</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-asian-marinade-for-chicken\"><strong>How to Make Asian Marinade for Chicken</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to infuse your chicken with a burst of flavor! This Asian marinade is simple, quick, and oh-so-delicious. With a preparation time of just 10 minutes, a cooking time of 15-20 minutes, and a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marination\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">marinating</a> time of at least 1 hour (or overnight for the best flavor), you’ll have a meal that’s sure to impress!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Asian-Marinade-for-Chicken.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making an asian marinade for chicken, including whisking ingredients, adding flavor boosters, marinating chicken, and grilling.\" class=\"wp-image-3369\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Asian-Marinade-for-Chicken.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Asian-Marinade-for-Chicken-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Whisk Together Ingredients</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a bowl, whisk together soy sauce, sesame oil, honey, and rice vinegar until well combined.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Add Flavor Boosters</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add minced garlic, grated ginger, chili flakes, and black pepper to the bowl. Stir to combine all those wonderful flavors.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Marinate the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place your chicken in a resealable bag or bowl. Pour the marinade over the chicken, ensuring it’s well coated.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Seal and Refrigerate</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Seal the bag or cover the bowl. Refrigerate for at least 1 hour, or overnight for maximum flavor.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Preheat Your Grill or Oven</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preheat your grill or oven to medium-high heat. Get ready for some sizzling action!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Remove and Shake Off Excess</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Take the chicken out of the marinade and shake off any excess. We want it flavorful, not swimming!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Cook the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Grill or bake the chicken until it’s cooked through and the internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C). You’ve got this!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 8: Garnish and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Garnish with sliced green onions and serve hot. Enjoy your delicious creation!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Asian</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>60 minutes (marinating)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>90 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>High Protein</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Hot with sliced green onions</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-asian-marinade-for-chicken\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Asian Marinade for Chicken</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Opt for fresh ginger and garlic for a vibrant flavor boost.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Marinate the chicken for at least 30 minutes, or overnight for deeper flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Balance the sweetness with a splash of lime juice for brightness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use low-sodium soy sauce to control saltiness without sacrificing taste.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with adding sesame oil for a nutty aroma.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-asian-marinade-for-chicken\"><strong>How to Serve this asian marinade for chicken</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve over a bed of fluffy jasmine rice for a comforting meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with steamed broccoli or bok choy for a fresh crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap in lettuce leaves for a fun, low-carb option.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with sesame seeds and green onions for a pop of color.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy in a stir-fry with colorful bell peppers and snap peas.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a side of coconut rice for a tropical twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use in a salad with mixed greens and a light sesame dressing.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can easily prepare and store your Asian marinade for chicken:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow the chicken to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place leftovers in an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Refrigerate for up to 3-4 days.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label the container with the date for easy tracking.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use freezer-safe bags or containers for best results.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Remove as much air as possible to prevent freezer burn.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for up to 2-3 months for optimal quality.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight before cooking.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Reheat in the microwave on medium power, stirring occasionally.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For stovetop, warm in a skillet over low heat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of water or broth to maintain moisture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Ensure the chicken reaches an internal temperature of 165°F (75°C).</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What&#8217;s a good Asian marinade for chicken?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>A great Asian marinade for chicken typically includes soy sauce, ginger, garlic, sesame oil, and a touch of honey or brown sugar for sweetness. This combination not only adds depth of flavor but also helps to tenderize the chicken, making it juicy and delicious. You can also add lime or lemon juice for a zesty kick!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What do Asians use to tenderize chicken?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Many Asian cuisines use ingredients like soy sauce, baking soda, or even pineapple juice to tenderize chicken. These ingredients contain enzymes or acids that break down proteins, resulting in a more tender texture. A common method is to marinate the chicken in a mixture of soy sauce and a bit of baking soda for about 30 minutes before cooking!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What do Chinese restaurants marinate their chicken in?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Chinese restaurants often use a marinade that includes soy sauce, oyster sauce, garlic, ginger, and sometimes a bit of sugar or honey. This mixture not only enhances the flavor but also gives the chicken a beautiful color when cooked. Some may also add sesame oil for an extra layer of flavor!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. How to make Chinese style marinade?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To make a Chinese-style marinade, combine soy sauce, ginger, garlic, sesame oil, and a sweetener like honey or brown sugar in a bowl. You can also add a splash of rice vinegar for acidity. Mix well and let your chicken marinate for at least 30 minutes, or up to overnight for maximum flavor. This simple marinade will elevate your chicken dishes to a whole new level!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now that you have this delightful Asian marinade for chicken, get ready to impress your taste buds! It’s simple, quick, and bursting with flavor. Picture a cozy dinner with loved ones, savoring every bite. So, roll up your sleeves, whip up this marinade, and enjoy the delicious rewards of your culinary adventure. Happy cooking!</p>\n",
